<%# Header account menu: who is signed in, and the account actions.

    design.md names this pattern - a native <details>/<summary> disclosure of links, not an
    ARIA menu widget with arrow-key roving. Native means it still opens without JS; the
    dropdown controller adds outside-click and Escape, and returns focus to the summary.

    Why it exists at all: nothing in the chrome said who was signed in. On a shared school
    Chromebook a student can land on a session someone else left open, and signing out was
    the last item in a sidebar that collapses behind a hamburger on a phone.

    No rule separates the identity block from the links - it sits on a slate-50 tint
    instead, so the panel groups without drawing a divider.

    Locals:
      extra_links - array of { label:, path:, data: } rendered above Sign out %>
<% item_class = "flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-slate-700 " \
                "hover:bg-slate-50 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 " \
                "focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary" %>

<%# data-testid because the sidebar's Trading floor disclosure is also a <details>/
    <summary>, so "the summary" is ambiguous in a test. %>
<details class="relative" data-controller="dropdown" data-testid="account-menu">
  <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-2 rounded-full py-1 pl-1 pr-2 hover:bg-black/5 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
    <%# The name is hidden below lg, so without this the control would have no accessible
        name there at all - the avatar and the chevron are both aria-hidden. %>
    <span class="sr-only">Account menu</span>
    <%= avatar_tag(current_user) %>
    <span class="hidden text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 lg:inline"><%= current_user.display_name %></span>
    <%= lucide_icon("chevron-down", class: "h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-slate-600") %>
  </summary>

  <div class="absolute right-0 z-20 mt-2 w-56 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white py-1 shadow-lg">
    <div class="bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">
      <p class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-slate-900"><%= current_user.display_name %></p>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600"><%= account_role_label(current_user) %></p>
    </div>

    <% local_assigns.fetch(:extra_links, []).each do |link| %>
      <%= link_to link[:label], link[:path], data: link[:data] || {}, class: item_class %>
    <% end %>

    <%= link_to "Sign out", destroy_user_session_path,
                data: { turbo_method: :delete },
                class: item_class %>
  </div>
</details>
